{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1092", "sample_idx": 46, "model_name": "google/gemma-3n-e4b-it", "content": "## Lost (and Found) in Japan\n\nJapan. The land of the rising sun. It lived up to every expectation and then some! Just got back from a whirlwind ten days and I'm already dreaming of returning.\n\nMy trip started in Tokyo, a dazzling explosion of neon lights, bustling crowds, and incredible food. Shibuya Crossing was as chaotic and captivating as everyone says. I spent hours wandering through quirky Harajuku, marveling at the fashion and street style. The food scene? Unbelievable. From Michelin-starred restaurants to tiny ramen shops tucked away in alleyways, every meal was a delight.\n\nNext up was Kyoto, a complete contrast to Tokyo. Ancient temples, serene gardens, and geishas gracefully gliding through Gion created a sense of timeless beauty. Fushimi Inari Shrine with its thousands of vibrant red torii gates was a truly unforgettable sight. I even participated in a traditional tea ceremony, a deeply calming and meditative experience.\n\nBeyond the cities, I took a day trip to Nara, where friendly deer roam freely in Nara Park. It was utterly charming!\n\nNavigating the train system was surprisingly easy, and the politeness of the Japanese people was truly heartwarming. While I only scratched the surface of what Japan has to offer, it’s a country that has completely stolen a piece of my heart. Definitely adding it to the top of my \"must-return\" list!\n", "logprobs": [{"token": "##", "logprob": -1.6689286894688848e-06}, {"token": "▁Lost", "logprob": -0.0011177966371178627}, {"token": "▁(", "logprob": -0.18502815067768097}, {"token": "and", "logprob": -8.344646857949556e-07}, {"token": "▁Found", "logprob": -0.0015026956098154187}, {"token": ")", "logprob": -0.1426810771226883}, {"token": "▁in", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": "▁Japan", "logprob": -0.11408442258834839}, {"token": "\n\n", "logprob": -0.25964632630348206}, {"token": "Japan", "logprob": -0.6041